nethack 3.0 is hard but not too hard! i've watched games where a player
will go clear across a floor to kill a cockatrice for the experience
points. the mentality seems to be kill everything in sight, forget about
Elbereth and ignore the inherent risks. those games seem to end up with
the player cursing that his armor or weapon is no good, that the monsters
are too powerful or that the game is too hard, etc. the most common
strategy flaw for these players seems to be getting in too deep (i.e. a
level 3 character cannot be expected to defeat a band of hill orcs
which you know will show up on level 4, or so). spoilers don't seem to
do much for these players. another strategy flaw seems to be applying
magic without a technique (i.e. it is not a good idea to quaff or read
as-discovered unknown potions or scrolls). after awhile you become
familiar with the effects of magic and better players develop a
technique for collecting/identifying/applying magic to minimize the
risks and maximize the utility of the magic. it seems that technique
cannot be taught ...

pre-nh3 versions of hack were tolerant of carelessness and
foolhardiness. nh3 is not and demands cleverness (more than luck) for
success. remember the hack maxim: behind every exit is an entrance.
to that i'd add that you are often your own worst enemy.

